-- Sample vector / hybrid queries against hybrid_search_demo.products
-- (table created by create_doris_table.sql, loaded by run-load.sh;
--  1M Amazon Home & Kitchen products embedded with BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5).
--
-- Run:   venv/bin/python doris-sql.py sample_query.sql
--
-- How it works
--   * `embedding` is ARRAY<FLOAT>(384) with an HNSW ANN index
--     (metric_type = inner_product). Vectors are L2-normalized, so
--     inner_product == cosine similarity: higher score = better match.
--   * The query text must be embedded with the SAME model and the BGE query
--     prefix. Get a vector literal for any text with:
--         ./run-search.sh --print-vector "your search text"
--   * inner_product_approximate(...) + ORDER BY ... DESC LIMIT k is the shape
--     the planner recognises as an ANN top-k and serves from the HNSW index.
--     Plain inner_product(...) is the exact (brute-force) version.
--   * Scalar predicates in WHERE are applied together with the ANN search
--     (hybrid search): equality / range on the metadata columns, and MATCH
--     on the inverted-indexed text columns.
--   * hnsw_ef_search (session variable, default 32) is the HNSW candidate
--     list size: raise it for better recall at the cost of latency.
--
-- The vector below is the embedding of the query
--   "insulated travel mug that keeps coffee hot for hours".

USE hybrid_search_demo;
SET hnsw_ef_search = 64;

